  "steps": {
    "_": "The order of the steps is the order of the lanes. A step names the places it runs between; where that depends on the journey, transport or fob overrides it -- fob first, then transport, then the plain pair. An override that has no entry for this journey falls through to the next, so a step can be told apart by island where it needs to be and by vehicle everywhere else. Every place named here needs a row in hours. A step may list what it was called before under was, so renaming one does not have to happen in two places at once. A step marked sticks:next keeps the gap it was written with to the step after it, so that when a later step is pushed it comes along rather than being left to sit. The order here is the fallback; where the sheet names a step, the sheet's row order wins, so the chart's rows are the sheet's rows.",
